module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LocalCohomology.BitUniformityIII.AmbientTwistMap
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.Existence
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.TwistDegreeOne
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# The map `𝒪_X(q+1) ⟶ 𝒪_X(q)` on the blowup lands in `I·𝒪_X(q)`

Let `A` be a commutative ring, `I ⊆ A` an ideal, `S = ⨁_{n ≥ 0} Iⁿ` the Rees algebra and
`X = Proj(S)` the blowup of `Spec(A)` in `I`. The map
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.ambientTwistMap` is the first map `𝒪_X(q+1) ⟶ 𝒪_X(q)` of
the second short exact sequence used in the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0GA7]. This file proves the one
thing about it that the *ideal-sheaf* model of the thickenings of the exceptional divisor cares
about: **its image is contained in `I·𝒪_X(q)`**, at every point of `X`.

That containment is the content of the identification `𝒪_X(1) = 𝒪_X(-Y)` of [Stacks, Tag 02OS]
part (3) in the direction in which it is a statement about the `Proj`-graded twists. It is the
comparison the ideal-sheaf model needs and the `Proj`-graded one does not supply: `𝒪_{Yₙ}` is
a pushforward along a closed immersion cut out by `I·𝒪_X`, not a `Proj`-graded object, so the
two families of twists have to be related by hand.

## The identity that does it

In the Rees model `S ⊆ A[X]` the map of the twists is division by `X`
(`Stacks.Blowup.reesShift`, which is `Polynomial.divX` on the truncation of `S(t+1)` above
degree `-t`, where it is `S`-linear). For `b ∈ I` the degree-one element `b⁽¹⁾ = bX` of `S` then
satisfies

`b⁽¹⁾ · divX m = bX · divX m = b · (X · divX m) = b · m`

for every `m` in the truncation, because an element of the truncation has vanishing constant
term (`Stacks.Blowup.coeff_zero_eq_zero_of_mem_reesTruncation`). That is
`Stacks.Blowup.reesDegOne_mul_reesShift`, and no hypothesis on `A` or on `I` enters.

Localise it. At a point `x` of `X` the degree-one elements `b⁽¹⁾`, `b ∈ I`, are not all in `x` —
the standard opens `D₊(b⁽¹⁾)` cover `X`, because `S` is generated in degree one
(`Stacks.Blowup.exists_reesDegOne_mem_primeCompl`) — so fix one that is invertible at `x`. The
identity then rewrites a degree-zero fraction `m / s` for the truncation of `S(t+1)` as

`divX m / s = (b⁽¹⁾ · divX m) / (b⁽¹⁾ · s) = b · (m / (b⁽¹⁾ · s))`,

with `m / (b⁽¹⁾·s)` a degree-zero fraction for `S(t)`: the degree bookkeeping works because
multiplying the denominator by a degree-one element is exactly the shift from `S(t+1)` to
`S(t)`. This is `Stacks.Blowup.map_reesShift_mk`, and
`Stacks.Blowup.exists_mem_degreeZeroModuleAt_map_reesShift` is its extension from the fractions
to the whole degree-zero localization, which is the stalk of `𝒪_X(t)` at `x` by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjStalkGlobalSections.associatedModuleSheafStalkEquiv`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Blowup.reesConst`: an element of `A = S₀` as a degree-zero element of the Rees
  algebra.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjStalkGlobalSections.degreeZeroFractions`: the degree-zero
  homogeneous fractions at a point of `Proj(S)`, the generating set of `degreeZeroModuleAt`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.stalkShift`: the stalk of the morphism `Stacks.Blowup.twistShiftMap` at a point
  of the blowup, read in the degree-zero localization.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Blowup.reesDegOne_mul_reesShift`: **multiplying `divX` by `b⁽¹⁾` is multiplying by
  `b`**, the algebraic form of [Stacks, Tag 02OS] part (3).
* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_reesDegOne_mem_primeCompl`: every point of the blowup has a degree-one
  coordinate coming from `I` invertible at it.
* `Stacks.Blowup.map_reesShift_mk`: the resulting identity on a degree-zero fraction.
* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_mem_degreeZeroModuleAt_map_reesShift`: **the image of
  `𝒪_X(t+1) ⟶ 𝒪_X(t)` lies in `I·𝒪_X(t)` at every point of the blowup**, read in the
  degree-zero localization.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjStalkGlobalSections.degreeZeroModuleAt_toAddSubgroup`: the
  degree-zero localization is the additive subgroup — not merely the span — generated by the
  degree-zero homogeneous fractions.
* `Stacks.Blowup.app_twistShiftMap`: the morphism `𝒪_X(t+1) ⟶ 𝒪_X(t)` on sections over an
  arbitrary open, the comparison isomorphism inverted followed by the map `divX` induces.
* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_mem_degreeZeroModuleAt_stalkMap_twistShiftMap`: **the containment for the
  morphism `Stacks.Blowup.twistShiftMap` itself**, on the stalk at a point of the blowup;
  `Stacks.Blowup.exists_mem_degreeZeroModuleAt_stalkShift` is the same statement through
  `stalkShift`, which is the form to use.

## Implementation notes

The scalars of `degreeZeroModuleAt` are the degree-zero fractions of the ring, which already
carry the generating set of homogeneous fractions into itself; so the span is an additive
closure, and `degreeZeroModuleAt_toAddSubgroup` records that once, in the generic graded
setting. Every statement here about the whole degree-zero localization is then proved by
`AddSubgroup.closure_le` on the generators alone, with no scalar step. This is not a
convenience: the scalar step has to transport the `Module.compHom` action of
`HomogeneousLocalization.AtPrime` through `LocalizedModule.map`, which is expensive at
`isDefEq`, and so are the additive and negation steps of the same induction when written with
`rw`. The conclusion is phrased against `AddSubgroup.comap` of `AddSubgroup.map` for the same
reason: the generators are then the only goal.

For the same reason the proof is cut into one declaration per step —
`mem_twistGrading_succ_of_mem_reesTruncationGrading` for the degree bookkeeping of the
numerator, `map_reesShift_mk` for the fraction identity, and
`exists_mem_degreeZeroModuleAt_map_reesShift_mk` for the two cases of the cut — rather than
written as one proof.

### The stalk bridge

Carrying the containment from `reesShift` to the *morphism* `twistShiftMap` is three existing
lemmas and no mathematics, but it is elaboration-sensitive: the cost sits in `stalkFunctor`'s
`map_comp` and in inferring the implicit stalk element. Three features of the spelling here
keep it affordable, in the order in which they matter:

* **The stalk functor is never applied to a composite.**
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.stalkMap` enters only through
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.stalkMap_germ`, which holds for *any* morphism of sheaves of
  modules; the factorisation of `twistShiftMap` is then performed on *sections*
  (`app_twistShiftMap`), where composition of morphisms of `SheafOfModules` is composition of
  functions and costs nothing. `stalkFunctor`'s `map_comp` never appears, and neither does the
  inverse of the comparison isomorphism as a morphism — only its action on one section.
* **No `rw` and no `subst` on anything mentioning the morphism.** `rw` with a germ identity whose
  sides mention `stalkMap _ x (twistShiftMap I t)` is prohibitively expensive at the motive
  check, and so is destructuring `associatedModuleSheafStalk_exists_germ` with `rfl`, whose
  substitution re-elaborates the goal. Both are replaced by an explicit `congrArg` with the
  function's type written out, the same remedy `ambientTwistMap` uses for `rw` on a morphism of
  `SheafOfModules`.
* **One occurrence of the composite per declaration.** What remains expensive is the
  identification of the hand-built stalk `associatedModuleSheafStalk` with
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.stalkObj`, which is definitional but not cheap and which the
  unifier redoes at every occurrence. The heartbeat budget is per declaration and a *statement*
  spends it before its proof begins, so two occurrences in one statement leave nothing for the
  proof. Hence `stalkShift` is a named definition, the work is done about it, and
  `exists_mem_degreeZeroModuleAt_stalkMap_twistShiftMap` writes the composite out once in a
  declaration whose proof is a single application.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GA6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GA6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GA7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GA7)
-/
@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Polynomial DirectSum
open AlgebraicGeometry
open AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj (twistingSheaf twistGrading integerGrading
  homogeneousSubmodule associatedModuleSheaf ModuleFiber)
open Stacks.GradedModule
open Stacks.GradedLocalization
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjStalkGlobalSections (degreeZeroModuleAt)

universe u v w z

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjStalkGlobalSections

attribute [local instance] ProjectiveSpectrum.isPrime

section Closure

variable {S : Type u} {M : Type v} {σ : Type w} {τ : Type z}
  [CommRing S] [AddCommGroup M] [Module S M]
  [SetLike σ S] [AddSubgroupClass σ S] (𝒮 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒮]
  [SetLike τ M] [AddSubgroupClass τ M] (𝒨 : ℤ → τ) [Decomposition 𝒨]
  [SetLike.GradedSMul 𝒮 𝒨]

/-- The homogeneous fractions of degree zero at a point of `Proj(S)`: the generating set of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjStalkGlobalSections.degreeZeroModuleAt`. -/
def degreeZeroFractions (x : ProjectiveSpectrum.top 𝒮) :
    Set (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.ModuleFiber (M := M) 𝒮 x) :=
  {z | ∃ (d : ℕ) (m : M) (s : x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl),
    m ∈ 𝒨 (d : ℤ) ∧ (s : S) ∈ 𝒮 d ∧ z = LocalizedModule.mk m s}

omit [AddSubgroupClass τ M] [Decomposition 𝒨] in
/-- **A scalar multiple of a degree-zero homogeneous fraction is again one.** The scalars are
the degree-zero fractions of the ring, so the degree bookkeeping is additive. -/
theorem smul_mem_degreeZeroFractions (x : ProjectiveSpectrum.top 𝒮)
    (r : HomogeneousLocalization.AtPrime 𝒮 x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal)
    {z : ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.ModuleFiber (M := M) 𝒮 x}
    (hz : z ∈ degreeZeroFractions 𝒮 𝒨 x) :
    HomogeneousLocalization.val r • z ∈ degreeZeroFractions 𝒮 𝒨 x := by
  obtain ⟨d, m, s, hm, hs, rfl⟩ := hz
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := HomogeneousLocalization.mk_surjective r
  have hnum₀ : (c.num : S) • m ∈ 𝒨 (c.deg +ᵥ (d : ℤ)) := SetLike.GradedSMul.smul_mem c.num.2 hm
  have hnum : (c.num : S) • m ∈ 𝒨 ((c.deg + d : ℕ) : ℤ) := by
    change (c.num : S) • m ∈ 𝒨 ((c.deg : ℤ) + (d : ℤ)) at hnum₀
    simpa only [Nat.cast_add] using hnum₀
  have hden : (c.den : S) * (s : S) ∈ 𝒮 (c.deg + d) := SetLike.mul_mem_graded c.den.2 hs
  have hcden : (c.den : S) ∈ x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl := c.den_mem
  refine ⟨c.deg + d, (c.num : S) • m,
    ⟨(c.den : S) * (s : S), x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl.mul_mem hcden s.2⟩,
    hnum, hden, ?_⟩
  rw [HomogeneousLocalization.val_mk]
  exact LocalizedModule.mk_smul_mk _ _ _ _

omit [AddSubgroupClass τ M] [Decomposition 𝒨] in
/-- **The degree-zero localization is the additive subgroup generated by the degree-zero
homogeneous fractions**, not merely their span: the generating set is already stable under the
scalars, by `smul_mem_degreeZeroFractions`. This is what lets a statement about the whole
degree-zero localization be proved by an induction with no scalar case. -/
theorem degreeZeroModuleAt_toAddSubgroup (x : ProjectiveSpectrum.top 𝒮) :
    (degreeZeroModuleAt 𝒮 𝒨 x).toAddSubgroup =
      AddSubgroup.closure (degreeZeroFractions 𝒮 𝒨 x) := by
  let : Module (HomogeneousLocalization.AtPrime 𝒮 x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal)
      (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.ModuleFiber (M := M) 𝒮 x) :=
    Module.compHom _ (algebraMap
      (HomogeneousLocalization.AtPrime 𝒮 x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal)
      (Localization x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl))
  have hscalar (r : HomogeneousLocalization.AtPrime 𝒮 x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal)
      {z : ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.ModuleFiber (M := M) 𝒮 x}
      (hz : z ∈ AddSubgroup.closure (degreeZeroFractions 𝒮 𝒨 x)) :
      r • z ∈ AddSubgroup.closure (degreeZeroFractions 𝒮 𝒨 x) := by
    induction hz using AddSubgroup.closure_induction with
    | mem z hz =>
      exact AddSubgroup.subset_closure (smul_mem_degreeZeroFractions 𝒮 𝒨 x r hz)
    | zero => simp
    | add z₁ z₂ _ _ ih₁ ih₂ => simpa only [smul_add] using add_mem ih₁ ih₂
    | neg z _ ih => simpa only [smul_neg] using neg_mem ih
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · change (degreeZeroModuleAt 𝒮 𝒨 x) ≤ Submodule.mk
      ⟨⟨AddSubgroup.closure (degreeZeroFractions 𝒮 𝒨 x), fun {_ _} => add_mem⟩, zero_mem _⟩
      (fun r _ hz => hscalar r hz)
    exact Submodule.span_le.2 fun z hz => AddSubgroup.subset_closure hz
  · exact (AddSubgroup.closure_le _).2 fun z hz => Submodule.subset_span hz

end Closure

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjStalkGlobalSections

namespace Stacks.Blowup

attribute [local instance] ProjectiveSpectrum.isPrime

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A)

/-- An element of `A = S₀`, read as a degree-zero element of the Rees algebra. -/
abbrev reesConst (b : A) : reesAlgebra I := algebraMap A (reesAlgebra I) b

/-- The element `reesConst I b`, viewed as a polynomial in `A[X]`, is the constant `C b`. -/
theorem coe_reesConst (b : A) : ((reesConst I b : reesAlgebra I) : A[X]) = C b := rfl

/-- **Multiplying `divX` by the degree-one element `b⁽¹⁾ = bX` is multiplying by `b`.**

This is the algebraic form of the identification `𝒪_X(1) = 𝒪_X(-Y)` of [Stacks, Tag 02OS]
part (3) on the blowup: on the truncation, where `divX` is linear, composing it with
multiplication by a degree-one generator returns the element multiplied by the corresponding
element of `I`. -/
theorem reesDegOne_mul_reesShift (t : ℤ) {b : A} (hb : b ∈ I) (m : reesTruncation I t) :
    (reesDegOne I hb) * (reesShift I t m : reesAlgebra I) =
      reesConst I b * (m : reesAlgebra I) := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  change (monomial 1 b : A[X]) * divX (((m : reesAlgebra I) : A[X])) =
    C b * ((m : reesAlgebra I) : A[X])
  rw [← C_mul_X_eq_monomial, mul_assoc,
    X_mul_divX_of_coeff_zero (coeff_zero_eq_zero_of_mem_reesTruncation I t m.2)]

/-- **Every point of the blowup has a degree-one coordinate coming from `I` invertible at it.**
The standard opens `D₊(b⁽¹⁾)`, `b ∈ I`, cover `Proj(S)`, because the Rees algebra is generated
in degree one. -/
theorem exists_reesDegOne_mem_primeCompl (x : ProjectiveSpectrum.top (reesGrading I)) :
    ∃ (b : A) (hb : b ∈ I),
      (reesDegOne I hb : reesAlgebra I) ∈ x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl := by
  obtain ⟨f, hxf⟩ : ∃ f : reesGrading I 1,
      x ∈ Proj.basicOpen (reesGrading I) ((f : reesAlgebra I)) := by
    have hcov := iSup_basicOpen_reesGrading_one_eq_top I
    have hx : x ∈ (⊤ : (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (reesGrading I)).Opens) := trivial
    rw [← hcov] at hx
    exact TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mp hx
  obtain ⟨b, hb, hfeq⟩ : ∃ (b : A) (hb : b ∈ I), (f : reesAlgebra I) = reesDegOne I hb := by
    refine ⟨((f : reesAlgebra I) : A[X]).coeff 1,
      by simpa [pow_one] using (f : reesAlgebra I).2 1, ?_⟩
    exact Subtype.ext (coe_eq_monomial I f.2)
  rw [hfeq] at hxf
  exact ⟨b, hb, (ProjectiveSpectrum.mem_basicOpen (reesGrading I) _ x).mp hxf⟩

/-- The numerator bookkeeping for the comparison below: an element of the truncation of
`S(t+1)` homogeneous of degree `d ≥ -t` is, read in `S(t)`, homogeneous of degree `d+1`. -/
theorem mem_twistGrading_succ_of_mem_reesTruncationGrading (t : ℤ) {d : ℕ}
    (hd : -t ≤ (d : ℤ)) (m : reesTruncation I t)
    (hm : m ∈ reesTruncationGrading I t (d : ℤ)) :
    (m : reesAlgebra I) ∈
      twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) t ((1 + d : ℕ) : ℤ) := by
  have hmt : (m : reesAlgebra I) ∈
      twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) (t + 1) (d : ℤ) := hm
  refine (mem_twistGrading_iff I (by push_cast; omega) _).mpr ?_
  have h1 := (mem_twistGrading_iff I (by omega) ((m : reesAlgebra I))).mp hmt
  have hidx : (((1 + d : ℕ) : ℤ) + t).toNat = ((d : ℤ) + (t + 1)).toNat := by
    push_cast; omega
  rw [hidx]
  exact h1

/-- **The fraction identity behind [Stacks, Tag 02OS] part (3).** A degree-zero fraction
`m / s` for the truncation of `S(t+1)` is carried by `divX` to `b` times the degree-zero
fraction `m / (b⁽¹⁾ · s)` for `S(t)`: multiplying numerator and denominator by `b⁽¹⁾` turns
`divX` into multiplication by `b`. -/
theorem map_reesShift_mk (t : ℤ) (x : ProjectiveSpectrum.top (reesGrading I))
    {b : A} (hb : b ∈ I)
    (hbx : (reesDegOne I hb : reesAlgebra I) ∈ x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl)
    (m : reesTruncation I t) (s : x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl) :
    LocalizedModule.map x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl (reesShift I t)
        (LocalizedModule.mk m s) =
      reesConst I b • LocalizedModule.mk ((m : reesAlgebra I))
        ⟨(reesDegOne I hb : reesAlgebra I) * (s : reesAlgebra I),
          x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl.mul_mem hbx s.2⟩ := by
  have hmul : (reesConst I b) • (m : reesAlgebra I) =
      (reesDegOne I hb : reesAlgebra I) • (reesShift I t m : reesAlgebra I) := by
    simp only [smul_eq_mul]
    exact (reesDegOne_mul_reesShift I t hb m).symm
  rw [LocalizedModule.map_mk, LocalizedModule.smul'_mk, hmul]
  exact (LocalizedModule.mk_cancel_common_left ⟨_, hbx⟩ s _).symm

/-- The degree-zero-fraction case of `exists_mem_degreeZeroModuleAt_map_reesShift`. -/
theorem exists_mem_degreeZeroModuleAt_map_reesShift_mk (t : ℤ)
    (x : ProjectiveSpectrum.top (reesGrading I)) {b : A} (hb : b ∈ I)
    (hbx : (reesDegOne I hb : reesAlgebra I) ∈ x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl)
    (d : ℕ) (m : reesTruncation I t) (s : x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl)
    (hm : m ∈ reesTruncationGrading I t (d : ℤ))
    (hs : (s : reesAlgebra I) ∈ reesGrading I d) :
    ∃ w ∈ degreeZeroModuleAt (reesGrading I)
        (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) t) x,
      LocalizedModule.map x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl (reesShift I t)
        (LocalizedModule.mk m s) = reesConst I b • w := by
  rcases lt_or_ge (d : ℤ) (-t) with hd | hd
  · have hbot := truncationAboveGrading_eq_bot (reesGrading I)
      (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) (t + 1)) (-t) hd
    have hm' : m ∈ truncationAboveGrading (reesGrading I)
        (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) (t + 1)) (-t) (d : ℤ) := hm
    rw [hbot, AddSubgroup.mem_bot] at hm'
    have hz0 : (reesShift I t) m = 0 := by
      rw [hm']; exact (reesShift I t).map_zero
    refine ⟨0, zero_mem _, ?_⟩
    rw [LocalizedModule.map_mk, hz0, smul_zero]
    exact LocalizedModule.zero_mk s
  · refine ⟨LocalizedModule.mk ((m : reesAlgebra I))
      ⟨(reesDegOne I hb : reesAlgebra I) * (s : reesAlgebra I),
        x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl.mul_mem hbx s.2⟩, ?_,
      map_reesShift_mk I t x hb hbx m s⟩
    have hden : (reesDegOne I hb : reesAlgebra I) * (s : reesAlgebra I) ∈
        reesGrading I (1 + d) :=
      SetLike.mul_mem_graded (reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I hb) hs
    exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨1 + d, (m : reesAlgebra I), _,
      mem_twistGrading_succ_of_mem_reesTruncationGrading I t hd m hm, hden, rfl⟩

set_option maxHeartbeats 400000 in
-- the proof elaborates `LocalizedModule.map` and graded-submodule closures over the Rees algebra
/-- **[Stacks, Tag 02OS] part (3) in the degree-zero localization at a point.**

At a point `x` of the blowup at which the degree-one element `b⁽¹⁾` is invertible, the map
`divX` of `Stacks.Blowup.reesShift` carries the degree-zero localization of the truncation of
`S(t+1)` into `b ·` (the degree-zero localization of `S(t)`). In other words the image of
`𝒪_X(t+1) ⟶ 𝒪_X(t)` lies in `I·𝒪_X(t)` at every point, which is the content of the
identification `𝒪_X(1) = 𝒪_X(-Y)` that any comparison of the `Proj`-graded model of the twists
with the ideal-sheaf model of the thickenings needs. -/
theorem exists_mem_degreeZeroModuleAt_map_reesShift (t : ℤ)
    (x : ProjectiveSpectrum.top (reesGrading I)) {b : A} (hb : b ∈ I)
    (hbx : (reesDegOne I hb : reesAlgebra I) ∈ x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl)
    {z : ModuleFiber (M := reesTruncation I t) (reesGrading I) x}
    (hz : z ∈ degreeZeroModuleAt (reesGrading I) (reesTruncationGrading I t) x) :
    ∃ w ∈ degreeZeroModuleAt (reesGrading I)
        (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) t) x,
      LocalizedModule.map x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl (reesShift I t) z =
        reesConst I b • w := by
  have hle : AddSubgroup.closure
        (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjStalkGlobalSections.degreeZeroFractions
          (reesGrading I) (reesTruncationGrading I t) x) ≤
      AddSubgroup.comap
        (LocalizedModule.map x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl
          (reesShift I t)).toAddMonoidHom
        (AddSubgroup.map
          (DistribSMul.toAddMonoidHom
            (ModuleFiber (M := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) x) (reesConst I b))
          (degreeZeroModuleAt (reesGrading I)
            (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) t) x).toAddSubgroup) := by
    refine (AddSubgroup.closure_le _).2 fun y hy => ?_
    obtain ⟨d, m, s, hm, hs, rfl⟩ := hy
    obtain ⟨w, hw, hwz⟩ :=
      exists_mem_degreeZeroModuleAt_map_reesShift_mk I t x hb hbx d m s hm hs
    exact AddSubgroup.mem_comap.2 (AddSubgroup.mem_map.2 ⟨w, hw, hwz.symm⟩)
  have hzc : z ∈ AddSubgroup.closure
      (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjStalkGlobalSections.degreeZeroFractions
        (reesGrading I) (reesTruncationGrading I t) x) := by
    rw [← Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjStalkGlobalSections.degreeZeroModuleAt_toAddSubgroup
      (reesGrading I) (reesTruncationGrading I t) x]
    exact hz
  obtain ⟨w, hw, hwz⟩ := AddSubgroup.mem_map.1 (AddSubgroup.mem_comap.1 (hle hzc))
  exact ⟨w, hw, hwz.symm⟩

/-! ### From `divX` to the morphism `twistShiftMap` -/

section StalkBridge

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjStalkGlobalSections
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSheafFunctoriality (associatedModuleSheafMap)
open TopologicalSpace (Opens)
open Opposite (op)

attribute [local instance_reducible] ProjectiveSpectrum.top
attribute [local implicit_reducible] TopCat.Sheaf sheafCompose

/-- **`twistShiftMap` on sections over an arbitrary open**: the comparison isomorphism inverted,
followed by the map `divX` induces. This is `twistShiftMap_eq` read on sections, by an explicit
`congrArg` whose function carries the type of the morphism; see the implementation notes. -/
theorem app_twistShiftMap (t : ℤ)
    (U : (Opens (ProjectiveSpectrum.top (reesGrading I)))ᵒᵖ)
    (s : (twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) (t + 1)).val.obj U) :
    (twistShiftMap I t).val.app U s =
      (associatedModuleSheafMap (reesGrading I) (reesTruncationGrading I t)
          (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) t) (reesShift I t)
          (reesShift_mem_twistGrading I t)).val.app U
        ((reesTruncationComparison I t).inv.val.app U s) :=
  congrArg
    (fun φ : twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) (t + 1) ⟶ twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) t =>
      φ.val.app U s)
    (twistShiftMap_eq I t)

/-- **The stalk of `twistShiftMap` at a germ, read in the degree-zero localization.** The value
is `LocalizedModule.map` of `Stacks.Blowup.reesShift` applied to the germ of the representing
section pulled back along the comparison isomorphism. Everything happens between *elements* of
stalks: the stalk functor is never applied to a composite. -/
theorem stalkEval_stalkMap_twistShiftMap_germ (t : ℤ)
    (x : ProjectiveSpectrum.top (reesGrading I))
    (U : Opens (ProjectiveSpectrum.top (reesGrading I))) (hx : x ∈ U)
    (s : (twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) (t + 1)).val.obj (op U)) :
    (associatedModuleSheafStalkEval (reesGrading I)
        (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) t) x
        ((AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.stalkMap _ x (twistShiftMap I t)).hom
          (associatedModuleSheafGerm (reesGrading I)
            (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) (t + 1)) x U hx s)) :
        ModuleFiber (M := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) x) =
      LocalizedModule.map x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl (reesShift I t)
        (associatedModuleSheafStalkEval (reesGrading I) (reesTruncationGrading I t) x
          (associatedModuleSheafGerm (reesGrading I) (reesTruncationGrading I t) x U hx
            ((reesTruncationComparison I t).inv.val.app (op U) s)) :
          ModuleFiber (M := reesTruncation I t) (reesGrading I) x) := by
  have hgerm₁ :
      (AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.stalkMap _ x (twistShiftMap I t)).hom
          (associatedModuleSheafGerm (reesGrading I)
            (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) (t + 1)) x U hx s) =
        associatedModuleSheafGerm (reesGrading I)
          (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) t) x U hx
          ((twistShiftMap I t).val.app (op U) s) :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.stalkMap_germ _ x (twistShiftMap I t) U hx s
  have hgerm₂ :
      (AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.stalkMap _ x
            (associatedModuleSheafMap (reesGrading I) (reesTruncationGrading I t)
              (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) t) (reesShift I t)
              (reesShift_mem_twistGrading I t))).hom
          (associatedModuleSheafGerm (reesGrading I) (reesTruncationGrading I t) x U hx
            ((reesTruncationComparison I t).inv.val.app (op U) s)) =
        associatedModuleSheafGerm (reesGrading I)
          (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) t) x U hx
          ((associatedModuleSheafMap (reesGrading I) (reesTruncationGrading I t)
              (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) t) (reesShift I t)
              (reesShift_mem_twistGrading I t)).val.app (op U)
            ((reesTruncationComparison I t).inv.val.app (op U) s)) :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.stalkMap_germ _ x _ U hx _
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (stalkMap_associatedModuleSheafMap_eval (reesGrading I)
    (reesTruncationGrading I t) (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) t)
    (reesShift I t) (reesShift_mem_twistGrading I t) x
    (associatedModuleSheafGerm (reesGrading I) (reesTruncationGrading I t) x U hx
      ((reesTruncationComparison I t).inv.val.app (op U) s)))
  refine congrArg (fun z : associatedModuleSheafStalk (reesGrading I)
      (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) t) x =>
    (associatedModuleSheafStalkEval (reesGrading I)
      (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) t) x z :
        ModuleFiber (M := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) x)) ?_
  exact hgerm₁.trans
    ((congrArg (fun y : (twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) t).val.obj (op U) =>
        associatedModuleSheafGerm (reesGrading I)
          (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) t) x U hx y)
      (app_twistShiftMap I t (op U) s)).trans hgerm₂.symm)

/-- **The stalk of `twistShiftMap` at a point, read in the degree-zero localization.**

A named definition rather than a composite written out: every occurrence of the composite makes
the unifier redo the identification of the hand-built stalk `associatedModuleSheafStalk` with
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.stalkObj`, and two such occurrences in one declaration exhaust
the heartbeat budget. `stalkShift_eq` is the way in. -/
def stalkShift (t : ℤ) (x : ProjectiveSpectrum.top (reesGrading I))
    (z : associatedModuleSheafStalk (reesGrading I)
      (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) (t + 1)) x) :
    ModuleFiber (M := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) x :=
  (associatedModuleSheafStalkEval (reesGrading I)
      (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) t) x
      ((AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.stalkMap _ x (twistShiftMap I t)).hom z) :
    ModuleFiber (M := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) x)

/-- The defining equation of `stalkShift`. -/
theorem stalkShift_eq (t : ℤ) (x : ProjectiveSpectrum.top (reesGrading I))
    (z : associatedModuleSheafStalk (reesGrading I)
      (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) (t + 1)) x) :
    stalkShift I t x z =
      (associatedModuleSheafStalkEval (reesGrading I)
          (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) t) x
          ((AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.stalkMap _ x (twistShiftMap I t)).hom z) :
        ModuleFiber (M := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) x) := rfl

/-- `stalkShift` on a germ, by `stalkEval_stalkMap_twistShiftMap_germ`. -/
theorem stalkShift_germ (t : ℤ) (x : ProjectiveSpectrum.top (reesGrading I))
    (U : Opens (ProjectiveSpectrum.top (reesGrading I))) (hx : x ∈ U)
    (s : (twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) (t + 1)).val.obj (op U)) :
    stalkShift I t x
        (associatedModuleSheafGerm (reesGrading I)
          (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) (t + 1)) x U hx s) =
      LocalizedModule.map x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl (reesShift I t)
        (associatedModuleSheafStalkEval (reesGrading I) (reesTruncationGrading I t) x
          (associatedModuleSheafGerm (reesGrading I) (reesTruncationGrading I t) x U hx
            ((reesTruncationComparison I t).inv.val.app (op U) s)) :
          ModuleFiber (M := reesTruncation I t) (reesGrading I) x) :=
  stalkEval_stalkMap_twistShiftMap_germ I t x U hx s

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 02OS] part (3) for the morphism `𝒪_X(q+1) ⟶ 𝒪_X(q)` itself**, stated through
`stalkShift`.

At a point `x` of the blowup at which the degree-one element `b⁽¹⁾` is invertible, every element
of the stalk of `𝒪_X(q+1)` is carried by `Stacks.Blowup.twistShiftMap` into `b ·` (the stalk of
`𝒪_X(q)`), read in the degree-zero localization. This is
`exists_mem_degreeZeroModuleAt_map_reesShift` transported from `reesShift` to the morphism; the
comparison isomorphism contributes nothing to the image. -/
theorem exists_mem_degreeZeroModuleAt_stalkShift (t : ℤ)
    (x : ProjectiveSpectrum.top (reesGrading I)) {b : A} (hb : b ∈ I)
    (hbx : (reesDegOne I hb : reesAlgebra I) ∈ x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl)
    (z : associatedModuleSheafStalk (reesGrading I)
      (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) (t + 1)) x) :
    ∃ w ∈ degreeZeroModuleAt (reesGrading I)
        (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) t) x,
      stalkShift I t x z = reesConst I b • w := by
  obtain ⟨U, hx, s, hs⟩ := associatedModuleSheafStalk_exists_germ (reesGrading I)
    (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) (t + 1)) x z
  obtain ⟨w, hw, hwz⟩ := exists_mem_degreeZeroModuleAt_map_reesShift I t x hb hbx
    (z := ((associatedModuleSheafStalkEval (reesGrading I) (reesTruncationGrading I t) x
        (associatedModuleSheafGerm (reesGrading I) (reesTruncationGrading I t) x U hx
          ((reesTruncationComparison I t).inv.val.app (op U) s))) :
        ModuleFiber (M := reesTruncation I t) (reesGrading I) x))
    (Subtype.mem _)
  exact ⟨w, hw, ((congrArg (stalkShift I t x) hs).symm.trans
    (stalkShift_germ I t x U hx s)).trans hwz⟩

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 02OS] part (3) for the morphism `𝒪_X(q+1) ⟶ 𝒪_X(q)` itself**, with the
composite written out: the image of `Stacks.Blowup.twistShiftMap` on the stalk at `x` lies in
`b ·` (the stalk of `𝒪_X(q)`), read in the degree-zero localization. -/
theorem exists_mem_degreeZeroModuleAt_stalkMap_twistShiftMap (t : ℤ)
    (x : ProjectiveSpectrum.top (reesGrading I)) {b : A} (hb : b ∈ I)
    (hbx : (reesDegOne I hb : reesAlgebra I) ∈ x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl)
    (z : associatedModuleSheafStalk (reesGrading I)
      (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) (t + 1)) x) :
    ∃ w ∈ degreeZeroModuleAt (reesGrading I)
        (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) t) x,
      (associatedModuleSheafStalkEval (reesGrading I)
          (twistGrading (S := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) t) x
          ((AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.stalkMap _ x (twistShiftMap I t)).hom z) :
          ModuleFiber (M := reesAlgebra I) (reesGrading I) x) = reesConst I b • w :=
  exists_mem_degreeZeroModuleAt_stalkShift I t x hb hbx z

end StalkBridge

end Stacks.Blowup

end
